doctype html
html(lang="en")
  head
    meta(charset="UTF-8")
    meta(name="viewport", content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0")
    title Focus Journal — Privacy Policy
    style.
      :root { --ink:#2b2b2b; --muted:#6f6f6f; --bg:#faf7f2; --accent:#b07b3e; }
      * { box-sizing:border-box; }
      body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink);
             font:17px/1.65 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; }
      main { max-width:44rem; margin:0 auto; padding:4rem 1.5rem 6rem; }
      h1 { font-size:2rem; margin:0 0 .25rem; }
      .updated { color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 2.5rem; }
      h2 { font-size:1.15rem; margin:2.25rem 0 .5rem; }
      a { color:var(--accent); }
      .back { display:inline-block; margin-top:3rem; color:var(--muted); text-decoration:none; }
  body
    main
      h1 Privacy Policy
      p.updated Focus Journal · Last updated 10 July 2026
      p Focus Journal is a private journaling app. This policy explains what the app does and does not do with your information.

      h2 What we collect
      p #[strong Nothing is collected by the developer.] Focus Journal has no analytics, no advertising, no third-party trackers, and no developer-operated servers that receive your data.

      h2 Your journal entries
      p Your entries and preferences are stored on your device. If you subscribe to Focus Journal Pro and are signed in to iCloud, they also sync through your own private iCloud account using Apple's CloudKit, and can be end-to-end encrypted with a key that only you hold. The developer cannot see, access, or retrieve your journal content.

      h2 Face ID &amp; biometrics
      p If you enable App Lock, the app uses Face ID, Touch ID, or your device passcode to unlock the journal. This authentication is handled entirely by iOS; the app never receives or stores your biometric data.

      h2 Notifications
      p If you turn on the daily reminder, the app schedules a local notification on your device at the time you choose. No data leaves your device to do this.

      h2 Purchases
      p Focus Journal Pro subscriptions are processed by Apple through the App Store. The app does not receive your payment details; subscription status is provided to the app by Apple.

      h2 Data deletion
      p Deleting the app removes its local data. To remove synced data, delete the app's data from iCloud in Settings → [your name] → iCloud → Manage Account Storage.

      h2 Children
      p The app is rated for general audiences and does not knowingly collect any data from anyone.

      h2 Contact
      p Questions about this policy: #[a(href="mailto:hello@tristanmatthias.com") hello@tristanmatthias.com]

      a.back(href="/") ← tristanmatthias.com
